[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3591850810","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113329#issuecomment-3591850810","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113329","id":3591850810,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7WF0s6","user":{"login":"SleepyMode","id":28950192,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4OTUwMTky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28950192?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepyMode","html_url":"https://github.com/SleepyMode","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepyMode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepyMode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepyMode/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepyMode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepyMode/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepyMode/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepyMode/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepyMode/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepyMode/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-29T18:22:34Z","updated_at":"2025-11-29T18:22:34Z","body":"I can replicate this somewhat.\nFirst of all, the bug completely disappears when the occluders are no longer touching:\n![Figure 1](https://i.imgur.com/S2yapsh.png)\n\nThis also doesn't seem to happen **at all** when you have a single occluder or any order that does not involve this exact combination.\nThis also disappears if you set the occluder to be slightly smaller than the object itself:\n![Figure 2](https://i.imgur.com/1SpETL8.png)\n\nSo basically, this happens when the occluder is being touched on all edges where it is visible, supposedly making it think it is occluded.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.gith